    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
    <p>I’m [artist name], an artist based in [home city]. I work in two mediums: oil paint and pencil.</p>
    <p>I paint in oil because it stays wet for days. That gives me time to move colour around, scrape it back and build the surface in layers until the light feels right. Oil lets me work slowly and change my mind, and the brush strokes stay in the finished painting.</p>
    <p>I draw in pencil because it is direct. Nothing sits between my hand and the paper, and every mark shows how it was made. Pencil keeps me honest about shape and tone, and many of my paintings begin as drawings.</p>
    <p>I paint [subjects the artist paints]. I started making work in [year started], and I am [training or self-taught].</p>
    <p>Every work on this site is an original. To ask about a piece or a commission, <a class="pencil" href="/contact/">contact me</a>.</p>
